r_max_depth (3.14): Name(...) past the depth, Name() without fields, else each field's"] [373 1 "// value, a list's or tuple's by astReprList, a node's one level deeper."] [419 1 "// astReprList is ast_repr_list: [] as repr, else the first and the last item (\"...\" between when more), a node one"] [420 1 "// level deeper."] [468 1 "// astSignature is a constructor's or product's __doc__ (asdl_c.py): NAME(TYPE[?*] FIELD, ...), NAME without fields;"] [469 1 "// Python.asdl's two \"expr?*\" sequences (Dict's keys, arguments' kw_defaults) as written there."] [517 2 "// AST's methods bind to the instance as method descriptors (methodDescrs; queue 202c: super().__init__ of a node"] [518 2 "// class's subclass, node.__replace__)"] [536 24 "// each node class's fields, for _field_types once every class exists"] [553 28 "// an optional attribute's default, at class level as CPython's"] [593 27 "// an optional field's default, at class level"] [614 2 "// a sum's __doc__ (asdl_c.py's visitSum): \"name = C1 | C2\" for a simple one, else one constructor a line"] [622 2 "// _field_types (CPython's add_ast_annotations: ast.dump reads it): a field's type, list[T] for a sequence, T | None"] [623 2 "// for an optional one (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 26] [93 32] [96 26] [128 37] [137 27] [147 122] [152 56] [176 73] [186 41] [195 36] [200 73] [213 23] [257 24] [278 24] [287 50] [289 33] [291 24] [325 37] [401 31] [407 23] [434 30] [636 26]]} (go/file "builtins_ast.go" :imports [


